u_entries:
docs/user-guide.md (this area writes it):
- the task budget paragraph: 'A task's own budget (New task, Budget) is what everything on the task may spend together: its runs, the critic's reviews of them and the fixes after a review. When the budget is large enough, each run keeps part of it for the review; when a review does not fit, the task pauses with its work kept, and Continue gives it what the review needs.';
- the estimate sentence: the estimate is what the task should cost in all, its review included, so a session's budget fits fewer tasks than before;
- the session review example: 'the planned tasks cost CHF 0.20 against an estimate of CHF 0.19'.

