How each item is built:
- Each item is confirmed failing before its fix; one that no longer fails goes to not_done with the evidence.
- One commit per item: the failing test first at the boundary its acceptance names, then the fix, then the siblings (validation rule 8).
- A stored figure is never asserted alone (rule 2). Each item also asserts what the person reads from it: the row's TaskCap words, the card's requestView(row) title, body and options, the session log line, the start-check figure.
- The composed cases run through composeRuntime with the Messages API stand-in priced as Sonnet 5.5 (budget-pause.test.ts' W15-13 harness), so the critic's calls are priced and prechecked as live.
- Restart cases (BA-2, BA-3, BA-7) compose the runtime twice on one home. Each awaits settleSessions before close and removes its homes with removeHomes (packages/runtime/test/helpers.ts:289, :307; ba9874a's Windows EBUSY fix; C3L-16).

