map.summary:
Scope: screens and person-facing words, read at ba9874a in /home/user/Forerunner, plus read-only views of fix/d1109-selftasks-run and fix/d1109-onerepo-join. Nothing was edited and no tests were run.

What run L3 built for L3-run-3 is one switch in TasksTab.tsx:87-102 (taskCapWords). While the row's cost (TaskView.spent, the ledger with reviews included, views.ts:455 and server.ts:1102-1113) reads the same as TaskView.actual (work only, views.ts:454), the line says "of CHF 0.20 budget". Once a review was paid it says "CHF 0.11 of CHF 0.20 budget left; reviews are not counted", or "CHF 0.20 budget used up; reviews are not counted". Both figures come from TaskView.cap, which is runCapOf = budget less actual (executor.ts:696-706, views.ts:437). The tooltip at TasksTab.tsx:73-74 says the critic's reviews are not counted. The rest of the money UI already shows the ledger figure, reviews included: the drawer header (TaskDrawer.tsx:156-157 "spent CHF X", which shows no budget), the drawer's per-run lines (TaskDrawer.tsx:343-346, including "Review by the critic · … · CHF X"), Costs > By task (CostsTab.tsx:154), and the Session page's "Tasks in this session" amounts (session-list.ts:802-828). The daemon's other budget words use the work-only figure but never say so: the Inbox card "It spent CHF X of its budget of CHF Y." and "It has spent CHF X, more than its estimate of CHF Y." (request-words.ts:872, 737, 750, fed by executor.ts:1793 and runner.ts:2878 = task.actual), the run's "Its budget of CHF 0.40 is spent (CHF 0.41 so far), so nothing ran." (executor.ts:984), "… CHF 0.24 in all" (budget-pause.ts:316, executor.ts:1788), and "This run may spend CHF X" (budget-pause.ts:345, figure from runCapOf). Their words stay true once the figure becomes the task's total. Only their source changes.

The sentences that state or imply work-only, or that split work from reviews:
- the row line and its tooltip (TasksTab.tsx);
- the session review's metrics line (views.ts:757-760);
- the critic's summary and overrun finding (packages/critic/src/session-review.ts:373, 715);
- user guide 1124-1129 and 1141-1143;
- ADR 0112 (166-167, 267-268, 373-380, 475-490) and ADR 0019:158-159;
- apps.md:100, runtime.md:2330-2333 and 2138-2148, critic.md:446-452, data-model.md:975.

Session-level sentences about the reserve ("a fifth kept for reviews") are about the session budget, not a task's. They stay true, but whether that reserve stays once estimates include reviews is an engine decision that changes the Start dialog words.

Chat says nothing about a task's budget or cost. The task line (project-facts.ts:80-111), task_get and recall_open (recall.ts:594-636) carry no money. The card line (project-facts.ts:310-353) carries the card's title and button labels ("paused at its budget of CHF 0.40", "Continue (CHF 0.40 more)"), which stay true. The recall 'spending' kind is project-level, "the work CHF X, chat about it CHF Y" (recall.ts:1093-1096). Its "work" already includes reviews, so it needs no change, but the word "work" means a different thing there than in the session review's breakdown.

Main risks for the screens:
- server.ts:1104 reads the task's ledger total filtered by projectId, so a task moved in by a join (OJ-02) would show less than a task_id-only budget counts.
- oneTaskView's fallback (server.ts:1117-1119) and recall's taskView (recall.ts:611-613) build TaskView without the ledger figure.
- spent can pass the budget slightly (a cut-off call, the late tail, Claude Code's limit set at cap+10%), so the row needs a 'used up' form.
- The fake daemon (fake-daemon.ts:936, 3617, 3623) still subtracts actual.
